.TH CFUNC 3 "July 13, 2026" "CAP5" "CAP5 Cluster Administration Package"
.SH NAME
cfunc \- shared bash function library for CAP5 tooling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source /usr/libexec/cap5/sh/cfunc
.br
.B source $CAPHOME/libexec/sh/cfunc
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfunc
is a bash function library sourced by
.BR deploy (1)
and available to any CAP5 tool script. It provides colored console
output, portable long-option CLI parsing, variable validation, package
search helpers, and the tool build/install driver used by
.BR deploy (1).
.PP
The library sets
.B "set -euo pipefail"
when sourced and initializes the global variables
.BR TOOL ", " PREFIX ", " RPM ", " CLEAN ", " DISTCLEAN ", and " DEBUG
to empty/zero defaults.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BI cinfo\ "MESSAGE..."
Print
.I MESSAGE
to stdout in bold blue. Informational output.
.TP
.BI cdebug\ "MESSAGE..."
Print
.I MESSAGE
to stdout in bold cyan. Debug output.
.TP
.BI cpass\ "MESSAGE..."
Print
.I MESSAGE
to stdout in bold green. Success output.
.TP
.BI cwarn\ "MESSAGE..."
Print
.I MESSAGE
to stdout in bold yellow. Warning output.
.TP
.BI cerror\ "MESSAGE..."
Print
.I MESSAGE
to
.B stderr
in bold red. Error output.
.PP
All five are wrappers around
.BR cprint (tag, " message..." ),
which only emits color codes when stdout is a terminal (via
.BR tput (1));
output is plain text when redirected or piped.
.TP
.BI parsecli\ "ARGS..."
Parse long-option CLI arguments and set the globals
.BR TOOL ", " PREFIX ", " RPM ", " CLEAN ", " DISTCLEAN ", and " DEBUG .
Resets all globals to defaults on every call, so results never leak
between invocations. Recognizes
.BR \-\-tool ,
.BR \-\-prefix ,
.BR \-\-rpm ,
.BR \-\-clean ,
.BR \-\-distclean ,
.BR \-\-debug " / " \-\-verbose ,
and
.BR \-\-help " / " \-\-usage
(the latter calls the caller-defined
.B usage
function and exits). Unrecognized flags print an error via
.B cerror
and call
.BR usage .
.TP
.BI check_validvar\ "NAME VALUE"
Returns 1 and prints an error via
.B cerror
if
.I VALUE
is empty or fewer than 2 arguments were given. Used to assert required
variables are set before proceeding.
.TP
.BI pkg_search\ "METHOD PACKAGE"
Search for
.I PACKAGE
using
.IR METHOD ,
one of
.BR yum ", " rpm ", " apt-cache ", " apt ", or " deb .
Returns 1 for an unrecognized method or fewer than 2 arguments.
.TP
.BI make_tool\ "TOOL [PREFIX]"
Locate the Makefile for
.I TOOL
under
.I /usr/src/cap5/TOOL
(system install) or
.IR $CAPHOME/src/TOOL
(development checkout), then build and install it according to the
.BR RPM ", " CLEAN ", and " DISTCLEAN
globals set by
.BR parsecli .
Exits 1 if neither location has a Makefile for
.IR TOOL ,
or if both
.B RPM
and a non-empty
.B PREFIX
are set simultaneously (unsupported combination).
This is the function
.BR deploy (1)
calls after parsing its CLI arguments.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CAPHOME
Path to the CAP5 development checkout. Consulted by
.B make_tool
when
.I /usr/src/cap5/TOOL
does not exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/cap5/sh/cfunc
System install location.
.TP
.I $CAPHOME/libexec/sh/cfunc
Development checkout location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deploy (1),
.BR bash (1)
